From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:34:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: keep the HDMI FRL bpp limits when raising the link
 rate

With HDMI_QUERY_FRL_HIGHEST_PIXEL_QUALITY, which NVKMS always uses, and
dsc_All_bpp, hdmiQueryFRLConfigC671() searches again at higher FRL rates. It
reset the bpp range to the full bppMaxX16, which undid the clampBpp limit of
8 bpp for 480 Hz and for 5120x2160 at 165 Hz, a client's forced bpp and the bpp
of a precalculated timing. With a forced FRL rate the search also started above
its end, and so went past that rate.

Keep the limit, leave forced and precalculated settings alone, and don't raise
the link rate when the bpp already is at the limit, as that gains nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/common/modeset/hdmipacket/nvhdmipkt_C671.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/modeset/hdmipacket/nvhdmipkt_C671.c b/src/common/modeset/hdmipacket/nvhdmipkt_C671.c
index 73194803..52c0fc1c 100644
--- a/src/common/modeset/hdmipacket/nvhdmipkt_C671.c
+++ b/src/common/modeset/hdmipacket/nvhdmipkt_C671.c
@@ -1349,13 +1349,17 @@ hdmiQueryFRLConfigC671(NVHDMIPKT_CLASS                         *pThis,
 
             if (pSinkCaps->pHdmiForumInfo->dsc_All_bpp)
             {
+                // A higher FRL rate only helps when it can raise the bpp. Keep bppMaxX16Itr: it holds the
+                // limit for this mode. Forced settings and precalculated timings must not change here.
                 if ((pClientCtrl->option == HDMI_QUERY_FRL_HIGHEST_PIXEL_QUALITY) &&
-                    (frlComputeResult.frlRate < (NvU32)dscMaxFRLRate))
+                    (frlComputeResult.frlRate < (NvU32)dscMaxFRLRate) &&
+                    !pClientCtrl->forceFRLRate &&
+                    (bppMinX16Itr != bppMaxX16Itr) &&
+                    (frlComputeResult.bppTargetx16 < bppMaxX16Itr))
                 {
                     // Increase FRL rate if possible and iterate over primary compressed format bppTarget to max Bpp
                     minFRLRateItr = getNextHigherLinkRate(frlComputeResult.frlRate);
                     bppMinX16Itr = frlComputeResult.bppTargetx16;
-                    bppMaxX16Itr = bppMaxX16;
                     bRedoDSCCalc = NV_TRUE;
                 }
 
